🚀 Just launched: FocusHub — Your Virtual Study Dojo!

Ever felt like your Zoom “study session” ends up being a scroll‑athon? I did. That’s why I built FocusHub, a real‑time, Discord‑meets‑Pomodoro platform for laser‑focused study and group study sessions.
This wasn’t just another side project—it was a hands-on crash course in building and deploying a production-ready, real-time web app.

🎯 Key Features:
- Live Study Rooms with WebSocket-powered chat  
- Pomodoro Timer with session logging  
- Lo-fi Music Player from static assets  
- Study Analytics Dashboard with session history, duration, and notes  
- Gamification: streaks, heatmaps, and leaderboards

🛠 Under the hood:
– Django + Channels (ASGI) served by Daphne on Render — so our chats never miss a beat.
– PostgreSQL in the cloud, with crazily simple deploys on Render Free Tier (yep, I even auto‑ran migrations in asgi.py to bypass SSH limits!).
– WhiteNoise for static files and careful CSRF/CORS lockdown so you only trust your own front‑end.

🔍 Lessons learned:
• How to architect real-time apps with Django and WebSockets
• The “small things” in deployment can break entire features (and cost hours to debug.) 
• Real-world debugging teaches more than any tutorial
• ASGI ≠ WSGI: real‑time needs a real‑time server (Daphne, not Gunicorn).
• CSRF and CORS are best friends keeping cookies safe and sound.
• Free‑tier hacks can be elegant (just less room for carelessness).

